          "message": "fix(site): TrustMedical story says what exists today, exactly\n\nXC1 NOT-YET on #560. The page described today's tools more strongly than the\ncode does.\n\n- Idea 4: the live check is a vote by independent model families. Matching a\n  quote against its source is the separate local `trustshell ground` command\n  (no model, no network), not part of the check (docs/api-reference.md).\n- Idea 3: a /check vote writes no score (lib/check-receipt.ts), so \"earn a\n  RepID from work that was checked\" is gone; the idea is future only and says\n  the rules do not exist yet. Titles for ideas 3 and 4 now say \"would\".\n- /vision TrustMedical card: \"opts in\", \"ever cross\", \"opens\" -> \"would\".\n- Footer link reads \"TrustMedical (vision)\"; the page and lib/site.ts comments\n  no longer say the footer is a way in (no page mounts Footer).\n- tests/trust-medical-page.test.ts: \"timeline\" and \"event\" added to the banned\n  words its header promised; new assertions pin the idea 3 and 4 sentences, the\n  /vision card, the footer label, and that the footer-comment stays true.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
